{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A command becomes a decision in two stages. First the owner replica allocates instance (r.Id, ++crtInstance[r.Id]) in handlePropose and startPhase1 derives the initial (seq, deps) from its conflict index and maxSeqPerKey, stores the record as PREACCEPTED, and broadcasts PreAccept to FastQuorumSize-1 preferred peers under thrifty or to all peers otherwise. Second each recipient validates the ballot against its own promise, recomputes (seq, deps) from its own conflict index while skipping the owner's own row when the recipient is not the owner, stores the command with status PREACCEPTED_EQ when nothing changed and PREACCEPTED when it did, and replies with (bal, vbal, Seq, Deps, CommittedUpTo, Status). The leader counts only replies whose ballot equals lb.lastTriedBallot, merges them with mergeAttributes (reply-wise maximum plus an equality flag), and commits immediately when preAcceptOKs >= FastQuorumSize-1 and the replies agreed and, for N>7, the merged deps are known committed, and the ballot is the initial ballot. Otherwise it records ACCEPTED, broadcasts Accept to a majority (N/2 peers when thrifty, all peers otherwise), counts acceptOKs and commits at acceptOKs+1 > N/2. The decision is then propagated as a Commit to every peer, which installs (Cmds, Seq, Deps, bal, vbal) and status COMMITTED.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B1-admit-propose\",\n        \"B2-phase1-attributes\",\n        \"B3-preaccept-recipient\",\n        \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n        \"B5-slow-path-accept\",\n        \"B6-commit-install\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F1-instance-record\",\n        \"F2-committed-decision\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S2-instance-bookkeeping\",\n        \"S5-broadcasters\",\n        \"S6-conflicts-watermarks\",\n        \"S7-attributes\",\n        \"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\",\n        \"S9-handlePreAccept\",\n        \"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\",\n        \"S11-handleAccept\",\n        \"S12-handleAcceptReply\",\n        \"S13-handleCommit\",\n        \"S15-handlePrepareReply\",\n        \"S19-durable-record\",\n        \"S25-defs-channels\",\n        \"S21-quorum-sizes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The authority context of an instance is a pair of ballots on the per-instance record: bal is the highest ballot promised to any leader for that instance and vbal is the ballot at which the record's current attributes were established. Every handler raises maxRecvBallot, and makeBallot derives the next ballot as id + k*N, shifted by another N when the replica is not the instance owner and raised past maxRecvBallot while IsLeader is set. Lower-ballot messages are dropped or answered without lowering a promise; a reply with a ballot higher than lb.lastTriedBallot counts as a nack, and once nacks exceed N>>1 an IsLeader replica makes a new ballot and runs prepare. Ownership of the instance row never moves, but the right to lead the instance does: startRecoveryForInstance, triggered by the execution timeout, rebuilds LeaderBookkeeping from the local record, raises bal and vbal to the new ballot and prepares against a slow quorum. The recovering leader then keeps the attributes reported with the highest vbal and either commits, accepts, try-pre-accepts, or restarts phase 1 with the recovered command or with NOOP when no command is known.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B9-recovery-trigger\",\n        \"B10-prepare-acceptor\",\n        \"B11-prepare-resolution\",\n        \"B12-try-preaccept\",\n        \"B14-ballot-monotonicity\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F6-ballot-priority\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S2-instance-bookkeeping\",\n        \"S4-execute-loop\",\n        \"S5-broadcasters\",\n        \"S7-attributes\",\n        \"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\",\n        \"S11-handleAccept\",\n        \"S14-recovery-start-prepare\",\n        \"S15-handlePrepareReply\",\n        \"S16-handleTryPreAccept\",\n        \"S17-find-conflicts\",\n        \"S18-handleTryPreAcceptReply\",\n        \"S21-quorum-sizes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"The two lines meet at the per-instance record. Formation consumes the dependency and sequence facts the conflict index (A6) establishes and produces the committed attribute vector; the authority line decides which candidate vector may be adopted, because a higher ballot lets a new leader re-propose but the value it must re-propose is selected by vbal. The support that stays eligible across a change of leader is therefore the highest-vbal reply among a slow quorum rather than the local record, and the support that a follower keeps is what it already stored for that instance. Once a record is COMMITTED with commands, recovery short-circuits (startRecoveryForInstance returns early) and later Commit messages for that instance are ignored, so established decisions constrain subsequent formation; a PreAccept for a record whose status is already >= ACCEPTED is deliberately not recomputed so accepted attributes are not regressed, and a lower-ballot PreAccept is dropped. Pending client proposals are carried in the leader bookkeeping across the transfer and are re-proposed when a NOOP commit lands on the owner's row. Old replies are rejected solely by ballot comparison, which is the only correlation between a reply and the round it belongs to. Execution (A5) closes the loop: it waits for every dependency instance to be COMMITTED, collapses cycles into one SCC executed in Seq order, and advances the contiguous watermarks that later proposals and recovery replies advertise through CommittedUpTo.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B3-preaccept-recipient\",\n        \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n        \"B6-commit-install\",\n        \"B7-execute-scheduler\",\n        \"B8-scc-closure\",\n        \"B11-prepare-resolution\",\n        \"B16-client-reply\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F1-instance-record\",\n        \"F2-committed-decision\",\n        \"F3-execution-prefix\",\n        \"F4-conflict-index\",\n        \"F5-pending-proposal\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S2-instance-bookkeeping\",\n        \"S4-execute-loop\",\n        \"S6-conflicts-watermarks\",\n        \"S7-attributes\",\n        \"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\",\n        \"S9-handlePreAccept\",\n        \"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\",\n        \"S12-handleAcceptReply\",\n        \"S13-handleCommit\",\n        \"S14-recovery-start-prepare\",\n        \"S15-handlePrepareReply\",\n        \"S19-durable-record\",\n        \"S20-exec\",\n        \"S21-quorum-sizes\",\n        \"S23-state-conflict-apply\",\n        \"S25-defs-channels\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"handlePreAccept's status >= ACCEPTED branch stores the incoming command in InstanceSpace[preAccept.LeaderId][Instance] while every other access in the same handler uses preAccept.Replica (S9-handlePreAccept); which histories reach that branch is unresolved.\",\n      \"handleAccept stores Deps, Seq, bal and vbal but never records an ACCEPTED status, so a replica in the accept quorum that never saw the PreAccept keeps Status NONE; the >= ACCEPTED guards in handlePreAccept and findPreAcceptConflicts therefore only ever see COMMITTED on non-leaders (S11-handleAccept, S9-handlePreAccept, S17-find-conflicts).\",\n      \"handlePrepareReply documents six sub-cases but the guards for sub-cases 3 and 4 are textually identical, so the TryPreAccept-based sub-case appears unreachable (S15-handlePrepareReply, S16-handleTryPreAccept).\",\n      \"handleTryPreAcceptReply's defer-cycle guard counts lb.possibleQuorum[tpar.AcceptorId] inside a loop over q, so the count can only be 0 or N and never equals N/2 (S18-handleTryPreAcceptReply).\",\n      \"recordInstanceMetadata writes bal and vbal into the same [0:4] byte range and stores Status at offset 4 inside a 9+4N header, and no reader of that format exists in the snapshot; the launcher always passes durable = false (S19-durable-record, S24-runReplica-epaxos).\",\n      \"the transconf branch inside Exec.strongconnect computes state.Conflict but performs no action, and run.go passes transconf = false (S20-exec, S24-runReplica-epaxos).\",\n      \"the N<=3 with Thrifty configuration skips the fast-path attribute-equality check while still committing at preAcceptOKs >= FastQuorumSize-1 = 1 (S10-handlePreAcceptReply, S21-quorum-sizes).\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core relationships are traced through real entry points (client propose to phase 1 to pre-accept replies to fast or slow decision to commit install, and ballot promise to nack-driven prepare to recovery sub-cases) and their connection is stated in terms of the per-instance record, the highest-vbal reply rule, the committed short-circuit and the ballot comparison that rejects old replies. The remaining questions are local anomalies inside handlers rather than missing formation, authority-transition or old-work handling, so the overview is recorded as usable with those anomalies kept as open_details and as the first Candidate's discriminator.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"49c847684d2a438fa43a53b3c9bca6d0\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"49c847684d2a438fa43a53b3c9bca6d0\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d8fd7f585e054fdba265f29c8f7bff4d\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n        \"disposition\": \"concrete_suspicion\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"direct_test\",\n        \"question\": \"When a replica receives PreAccept for instance (Replica, Instance) while its local record for that instance already has Status >= ACCEPTED but stores no commands, handlePreAccept writes the received command into InstanceSpace[preAccept.LeaderId][Instance] instead of the addressed instance InstanceSpace[preAccept.Replica][Instance]. Is any legal history able to put a replica in that state with preAccept.LeaderId != preAccept.Replica, and if so does the addressed record (Replica, Instance) stay without commands (halting its row's execution and the recovery replies about it) while an unrelated record (LeaderId, Instance) acquires a command that no quorum committed for it?\",\n        \"importance\": \"Wrong-slot attribution of a command mutates protocol state without any quorum behind it: a record that never committed that command can become executable as though it had, while the record the message was addressed to can be left permanently unexecutable because executeCommands requires Cmds != nil and findSCC returns false for a command-less instance. Both effects are consensus-visible (an uncommitted command can reach the state machine, and a committed instance can stop making progress).\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S9-handlePreAccept\",\n          \"S11-handleAccept\",\n          \"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\",\n          \"S12-handleAcceptReply\",\n          \"S13-handleCommit\",\n          \"S15-handlePrepareReply\",\n          \"S16-handleTryPreAccept\",\n          \"S20-exec\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [],\n        \"objects\": [],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"instance owned by replica R and led by replica L != R (recovery re-proposal)\",\n          \"instance owned and led by the same replica (normal proposal) as the control that must behave identically\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"deliver PreAccept(LeaderId=L, Replica=R, Instance=i, Ballot=b, Command=c, Seq, Deps) to a replica whose InstanceSpace[R][i] has Status >= ACCEPTED and Cmds == nil\",\n          \"compare the record that receives Cmds after the handler returns against the record named by (Replica, Instance)\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B3-preaccept-recipient\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F1-instance-record\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B5-slow-path-accept\": \"shows that the accept phase stores accepted attributes on followers without any status transition, which is the premise the >= ACCEPTED branch would need\",\n          \"B11-prepare-resolution\": \"re-runs pre-accept on behalf of another replica's instance, which is the only read path in which PreAccept.LeaderId differs from PreAccept.Replica\",\n          \"B12-try-preaccept\": \"another recovery path that re-sends a command for an instance owned by a different replica\",\n          \"B7-execute-scheduler\": \"shows the execution requirement Cmds != nil that makes a command-less record of the addressed instance a permanent row stall\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"preservation\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"no read path found so far sets Status >= ACCEPTED together with Cmds == nil on a replica that did not already hold the command: leader-side transitions copy lb.cmds, handleCommit copies commit.Command, and a nil Command does not survive the wire format as nil (S10-handlePreAcceptReply, S12-handleAcceptReply, S13-handleCommit)\",\n          \"handleAccept deliberately stores accepted attributes without a status transition, which would make the branch unreachable for acceptors rather than wrong (S11-handleAccept)\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether any in-repository path (for example a recovery that commits an instance for which no replica reported a command) can leave Status >= ACCEPTED with Cmds == nil at a replica\",\n          \"whether the branch was intended to address the instance owner and the LeaderId index is the only wrong part, or whether the accepted-state condition is also wrong\",\n          \"whether an executor can observe the wrong-slot write, since executeCommands requires Cmds != nil and Status == COMMITTED for the affected record\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 2,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Source reading showed the discrepancy directly: S9-handlePreAccept uses preAccept.Replica at lines 782, 792-798, 810, 816 and 828-829, but preAccept.LeaderId at line 809 for the same object. The state needed to reach the branch (Status >= ACCEPTED with nil Cmds on a replica receiving a PreAccept) is not obviously produced by any path read so far: handleAccept stores bal/vbal/Seq/Deps without recording ACCEPTED (S11-handleAccept), the leader-side ACCEPTED/COMMITTED transitions set Cmds from lb.cmds (S10-handlePreAcceptReply, S12-handleAcceptReply), handleCommit installs commit.Command (S13-handleCommit), and a marshalled nil command slice comes back as a non-nil empty slice. The Candidate therefore fixes the reachability premise as the discriminator rather than assuming the defect is triggered.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"active\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stop_reason\": \"First substantive product of this run: a partial but usable map of the EPaxos replica responsibility (core_overview for both core relationships, seven activities, sixteen behaviors, seven facts, ten surfaced unread boundaries) plus the first Candidate. The map is sourced only from the captured snapshot; all anomalies found while tracing the backbone are retained as open_details instead of being asserted as defects. The Candidate selects the one sourced discrepancy that would matter most if reachable: handlePreAccept stores a received command into InstanceSpace[PreAccept.LeaderId][Instance] while every other access in the same handler addresses the instance (PreAccept.Replica, Instance) named by the message.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": null,\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [],\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"executions\": [],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"d8fd7f585e054fdba265f29c8f7bff4d\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"units\": [],\n  \"claims\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [],\n  \"assessments\": [],\n  \"frontier\": {\n    \"relationships\": [\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F1-instance-record\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S2-instance-bookkeeping\",\n          \"S9-handlePreAccept\",\n          \"S13-handleCommit\",\n          \"S15-handlePrepareReply\",\n          \"S19-durable-record\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether replacing bal, vbal, Seq and Deps on a record that already stored accepted attributes can lose an accepted value a later recovery depends on\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B2-phase1-attributes\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B3-preaccept-recipient\",\n          \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n          \"B5-slow-path-accept\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\",\n          \"B9-recovery-trigger\",\n          \"B10-prepare-acceptor\",\n          \"B11-prepare-resolution\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B10-prepare-acceptor\",\n          \"B11-prepare-resolution\",\n          \"B2-phase1-attributes\",\n          \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n          \"B5-slow-path-accept\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\",\n          \"B9-recovery-trigger\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": [\n          \"d8fd7f585e054fdba265f29c8f7bff4d\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F2-committed-decision\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S10-handlePreAcceptReply\",\n          \"S12-handleAcceptReply\",\n          \"S13-handleCommit\",\n          \"S15-handlePrepareReply\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether every ordering of committed attributes a follower can install is also reachable as a decision by some quorum\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n          \"B5-slow-path-accept\",\n          \"B11-prepare-resolution\",\n          \"B12-try-preaccept\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\",\n          \"B16-client-reply\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B11-prepare-resolution\",\n          \"B12-try-preaccept\",\n          \"B16-client-reply\",\n          \"B4-fast-path-decision\",\n          \"B5-slow-path-accept\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F3-execution-prefix\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S4-execute-loop\",\n          \"S6-conflicts-watermarks\",\n          \"S20-exec\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B7-execute-scheduler\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B16-client-reply\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B16-client-reply\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B7-execute-scheduler\",\n          \"B8-scc-closure\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F4-conflict-index\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S6-conflicts-watermarks\",\n          \"S7-attributes\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether a restart with empty instance space and empty conflict tables is a supported configuration\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B2-phase1-attributes\",\n          \"B3-preaccept-recipient\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\",\n          \"B13-conflict-index-update\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B12-try-preaccept\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B12-try-preaccept\",\n          \"B13-conflict-index-update\",\n          \"B2-phase1-attributes\",\n          \"B3-preaccept-recipient\",\n          \"B6-commit-install\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F5-pending-proposal\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S8-handlePropose-startPhase1\",\n          \"S13-handleCommit\",\n          \"S14-recovery-start-prepare\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether the re-proposal path can duplicate a command that was already committed\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B1-admit-propose\"\n        ],\n        \"consumers\": [\n          \"B9-recovery-trigger\",\n          \"B16-client-reply\"\n        ],\n        \"invalidators\": [],\n        \"reinterpreters\": [],\n        \"unreferenced_behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B1-admit-propose\",\n          \"B16-client-reply\",\n          \"B9-recovery-trigger\"\n        ],\n        \"coverage\": \"Described relationships; selected checks settle only their explicit scope\",\n        \"candidate_ids\": []\n      },\n      {\n        \"fact_id\": \"F6-ballot-priority\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S14-recovery-start-prepare\",\n          \"S15-handlePrepareReply\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"whether the recovering leader's own record is adequately represented when its vbal was just overwritten with the new ballot\"\n        ],\n        \"producers\": [\n          \"B9-recovery-trigger\",\n         